+
+Both multi-link models recovered in all six held-out combinations of perturbation direction, torque, and sensory delay, including opposite \qty{20}{\newton\meter} diagonal disturbances with \qty{32}{\milli\second} delay. Across those trials, the longest settling times were \qty{0.612}{\second} for two links and \qty{0.805}{\second} for three. Settling required every joint to remain within \ang{1} of upright and below \qty{5}{\degree\per\second} for \qty{0.5}{\second}. The fixed base prevents a fall through loss of foot contact. When the premotor circuitry was transferred to the Gait2392 standing model, its virtual pelvic harness still carried more than \qty{70}{\percent} of body weight. The pendulums thus provide a test of postural control before adding foot contact and body-weight transfer.
